content.text:
Now reload, start, autoplay script. To automate hits, we need a loop that presses lane shortly before note time. Expose battle; in eval:

```
const b = window.__BEATFALL__.battle; // after start
```

We can inject an autoplayer that uses setInterval:
```
window.__auto = setInterval(()=>{
 const b=window.__BEATFALL__.battle; if(!b) return;
 const t=b.songTime();
 for(const n of b.notes){ if(n.head==='pending' && n.time - t < 0.025 && n.time - t > -0.02){ b.pressLane(n.lane); break; } }
 if(b.fever>=100) b.activateFever();
}, 8);
```
But multiple notes same time (chords) need press each lane. Iterate all pending within window and press each (avoid repeat: press marks head hit immediately, so fine).

Use interval 6ms; the press hit window wide enough (perfect 68ms). Timing from setInterval jitter ~ few ms.

Also hold sustain: need laneHold >0; pressLane doesn't increment laneHold (that's from input). So holds won't tick. For autoplay, increment b.laneHold[lane]++ after press; but never release; laneHold persists and affects future holds positively. Fine for test. Actually battle input increments laneHold then pressLane; for auto, do b.laneHold[lane]++.

Let's reload, start, inject at 1s, wait ~25s, screenshot mid-battle; then wait until victory/reward. Could automate whole run multiple floors? Later.

Careful: headless browser tab may throttle rAF when not focused? Playwright page is visible, fine. Audio context may be running (headless with no audio device?) WebAudio works with SwiftShader? Audio may fail in headless but ctx still runs. We saw battle time progressed (misses), so yes.

Also audio might be in suspended state if not activated? It progressed (ctx running). Good.

Let's run.

