Fix hold tail clamping:
```
const tailTop = Math.max(-80, tailY);
const tailBottom = Math.max(tailTop + 1, y);
if (y > -60) draw...
```
Simplest:
```
const tailTop = Math.max(-60, tailY);
const tailH = y - tailTop;
if (tailH > 2) { draw rr(...), stroke, cap if tailY > -60 }
```
Also for sustain body of hit holds: topY can be positive; hitY - topY >0 always. topY can be < -many, fine, height positive. No issue.

Also `rr` helper could guard r negative with Math.max(0, ...). But the height negative is the real issue; adding `if (h < 0) return` in rr would avoid exceptions but hide logic. Do both: ensure w/h positive in rr (return) and fix tail.

Let's patch.

